IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp5-months`
IMPORT `cp5-d-retirement`
IMPORT `cp5-d-disability`
IMPORT `cp5-d-reinstatement`
IMPORT `cp5-d-death-survivor`
IMPORT `cp5-d-child`
IMPORT `cp5-d-post-retirement`
IMPORT `cp5-e-amount`
IMPORT `cp5-f-appeals`
IMPORT `cp5-g-general`
IMPORT `cp5-related-provisions`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part II, Divisions D to G, and the Related Provisions: THE SEAT LAYER (piece cp5).
--
-- SEAT: a worker, self-employed person, survivor, child or person with a disability who contributes to or may claim from the
-- Canada Pension Plan, asking whether and how much they must contribute, whether they qualify for a retirement pension or a
-- disability, survivor's or children's benefit, how much, and what they must do or tell the Minister. This range
-- (benefits: special rules, the share payable under the Act, reconsideration and appeal, offences and inspections) answers:
-- from which month a benefit is paid and until which; what is owed to the person or can be done to them; and by when to act.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs: yes/no, dates, numbers and choices from a list. A rule of the long modules
-- that takes an optional day (MAYBE DATE) is fed from a yes/no and a day (the helper below). A date of birth is asked, never an
-- age: the long modules route every age through section 2(2). A month is asked as any day in that month.
-- Where the Act leaves a judgment to the Minister or a court, the question asks whether it has been made ("Has the Minister
-- been satisfied that ...?"); nothing is guessed.
-- A question answers NOTHING (shown as no value) where the Act does not decide the case; NOTES.md, "What the text turns out to say".
--
-- The Regulations' figures that the long modules read (regulation 64: 60 days, $2,387; regulation 71: 12 months; regulation 74.1:
-- 365 days; regulation 74.2; regulation 51; regulation 65.1) are built into the answers: the person is not asked them.
-- A change to one of those regulations would change these answers.
-- The persons the Act treats as officials (the Minister, the judge, the Tribunal) have no seat: their duties appear as what the
-- person is owed (written reasons, back payment) and their powers as what can be done to the person.
--
-- The individual's seat is the only seat of this piece. An estate (an "applicant" that is not an individual) is not asked about,
-- so the long modules' field "the applicant is an estate" is fixed at FALSE below.

§ `Canada Pension Plan -- Part II, Divisions D to G: the questions of a contributor, survivor, child or person with a disability`

-- Plumbing, not law: a yes/no and a day become an optional day for the long modules.
GIVEN present IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` present day MEANS
    IF present THEN JUST day ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Retirement pension -- when it starts and how long it is paid`

-- s 67. The month from which the retirement pension is paid, under whichever of subsections (1), (2), (3), (3.1) and (3.2) governs.
-- The pre-1987 facts (the last month you worked and made a contribution, the last month with earnings attributed under section 55)
-- are read only by subsection (1), for a pension that started before 1987.
@export From which month is my retirement pension paid (s 67)?
GIVEN `my retirement pension has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister approved payment of your retirement pension? (If not, the Act does not say from which month it will be paid.)
      `the day my retirement pension was approved` IS A DATE @desc On what day was payment of your retirement pension approved? (Ignored if it has not been approved; if you are asking what would happen once it is, give today's date.)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day my application was received` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Minister receive your application for the retirement pension?
      `I chose a month in my application for the pension to start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you choose, in your application, a month for the pension to start?
      `a day in the month I chose` IS A DATE @desc Which month did you choose? (Give any day in that month; ignored if you chose none.)
      `I have wholly or substantially stopped paid employment and self-employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you wholly or substantially stopped being engaged in paid employment and self-employment?
      `the day I stopped` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you wholly or substantially stop? (Ignored if you have not.)
      `I have a last month in which I worked and made a contribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a pension that started before 1987: is there a last month in which you worked and for which a contribution was made under the Act or a provincial pension plan?
      `a day in the last month I worked and made a contribution` IS A DATE @desc Only for a pension that started before 1987: which month was that? (Any day in it.)
      `I have a last month with earnings attributed under section 55` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a pension that started before 1987: is there a last month for which unadjusted pensionable earnings were attributed to you under section 55 (division of pensionable earnings between spouses)?
      `a day in the last month with earnings attributed under section 55` IS A DATE @desc Only for a pension that started before 1987: which month was that? (Any day in it.)
      `the requirement to make an application was waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister waive the requirement that you apply for the retirement pension (possible only from age 70)?
      `the day the requirement was waived` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the requirement waived? (Ignored if it was not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From which month is my retirement pension paid (s 67)` IS
    `s 67 — the month a retirement pension is first payable` application waived
    WHERE
        application MEANS `cp5 Application for a retirement pension` WITH
            -- an individual, not an estate: the seat is the individual's
            `the applicant is an estate` IS FALSE
            `date of birth of the applicant` IS `my date of birth`
            `day the application was received` IS `the day my application was received`
            `day payment of the pension was approved` IS `cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `my retirement pension has been approved` `the day my retirement pension was approved`
            `a day in the month the contributor last worked and for which a contribution was made` IS `cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `I have a last month in which I worked and made a contribution` `a day in the last month I worked and made a contribution`
            `a day in the last month for which unadjusted pensionable earnings were attributed under section 55` IS `cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `I have a last month with earnings attributed under section 55` `a day in the last month with earnings attributed under section 55`
            `a day in the month the applicant chose for the pension to commence` IS `cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `I chose a month in my application for the pension to start` `a day in the month I chose`
            `day the applicant wholly or substantially ceased paid employment and self-employment` IS `cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `I have wholly or substantially stopped paid employment and self-employment` `the day I stopped`
        waived MEANS `cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `the requirement to make an application was waived` `the day the requirement was waived`

-- s 68. A retirement pension is paid for the lifetime of the beneficiary, through the month of death.
@export Is a retirement pension paid for a particular month (s 68)?
GIVEN `the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? (Any day in that month.)
      `the first month for which the pension is payable` IS A DATE @desc From which month is the pension payable? (Any day in that month.)
      `the beneficiary has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person who received the retirement pension died?
      `the day the beneficiary died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did they die? (Ignored if they have not.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a retirement pension paid for a particular month (s 68)` IF
    `s 68 — a retirement pension is paid for a month` `the month I am asking about` `the first month for which the pension is payable` (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `the beneficiary has died` `the day the beneficiary died`)

-- s 67(4). Applying for a retirement pension after a disability pension has stopped: the application is treated as received in an earlier month.
-- Situation: your disability pension has stopped because the decision that you were disabled was reversed or you ceased to be disabled.
@export In which month is my application for a retirement pension treated as received, after my disability pension stopped (s 67(4))?
GIVEN `my disability pension is no longer payable because the decision that I was disabled was reversed or I ceased to be disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your disability pension no longer payable because the decision that you were disabled was reversed, or because you ceased to be disabled?
      `the day I was notified that my disability pension had ceased` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you notified that your disability pension had ceased?
      `the day I applied for a retirement pension` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you apply for a retirement pension?
      `the Minister allowed me a longer period to apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister allow you a period longer than 90 days after the notice in which to apply?
      `the last day of that longer period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the longer period? (Ignored if none.)
      `a day in the month my disability pension application was made` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you apply for the disability pension? (Any day in that month.)
      `a day in the last month my disability pension was payable` IS A DATE @desc What was the last month for which the disability pension was payable? (Any day in that month.)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `In which month is my application for a retirement pension treated as received, after my disability pension stopped (s 67(4))` IS
    `s 67(4) — the month in which the application for a retirement pension is deemed to have been received` `my disability pension is no longer payable because the decision that I was disabled was reversed or I ceased to be disabled` `the day I was notified that my disability pension had ceased` `the day I applied for a retirement pension` (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `the Minister allowed me a longer period to apply` `the last day of that longer period`) `a day in the month my disability pension application was made` `a day in the last month my disability pension was payable` `my date of birth`

§§ `Disability pension and post-retirement disability benefit -- when they start, how long they last and when they end`
-- Situation: you are disabled, or have applied for a disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit.

-- s 69. The month a disability pension is first payable.
@export From which month is my disability pension payable (s 69)?
GIVEN `payment of my disability pension has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister approved payment of your disability pension?
      `a day in the month I became disabled` IS A DATE @desc In which month were you determined to have become disabled? (Any day in that month.)
      `I received a disability pension in the five years before that month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At any time in the five years before the month you became disabled, did you receive a disability pension under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From which month is my disability pension payable (s 69)` IS
    `s 69 — the month a disability pension is first payable` `payment of my disability pension has been approved` `a day in the month I became disabled` `I received a disability pension in the five years before that month`

-- s 69(b). The look-back for the date of disability: twelve months instead of fifteen after a recent disability pension.
@export How many months before my application can I be treated as having become disabled (s 69(b))?
GIVEN `I received a disability pension in the five years before the month I became disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At any time in the five years before the month you became disabled, did you receive a disability pension under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many months before my application can I be treated as having become disabled (s 69(b))` IS
    `s 69(b) — the number of months to read in place of fifteen months in paragraph 42(2)(b)` `I received a disability pension in the five years before the month I became disabled`

-- s 70(1). The last month for which a disability pension is paid.
@export Until which month is my disability pension paid (s 70(1))?
GIVEN `I have ceased to be disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ceased to be disabled?
      `a day in the month I ceased to be disabled` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you cease to be disabled? (Any day in it; ignored if you have not.)
      `I have started a retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a retirement pension under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan payable to you?
      `the first month for which my retirement pension is payable` IS A DATE @desc From which month is the retirement pension payable? (Any day in that month; ignored if none.)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `I have died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person who received the pension died?
      `the day they died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did they die? (Ignored if not.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Until which month is my disability pension paid (s 70(1))` IS
    `s 70(1) — the last month for which a disability pension is payable` (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `I have ceased to be disabled` `a day in the month I ceased to be disabled`) (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `I have started a retirement pension` `the first month for which my retirement pension is payable`) `my date of birth` (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `I have died` `the day they died`)

-- s 70(2). Reaching 65 ends the disability pension and is treated as applying for the retirement pension.
@export Does my disability pension end because I reach 65 (s 70(2))?
GIVEN `I have ceased to be disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ceased to be disabled?
      `a day in the month I ceased to be disabled` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you cease to be disabled? (Any day in it; ignored if you have not.)
      `I have started a retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a retirement pension under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan payable to you?
      `the first month for which my retirement pension is payable` IS A DATE @desc From which month is the retirement pension payable? (Any day in that month; ignored if none.)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `I have died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person who received the pension died?
      `the day they died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did they die? (Ignored if not.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my disability pension end because I reach 65 (s 70(2))` IF
    `s 70(2) — the disability pension ceases to be payable by reason of the beneficiary having reached 65` (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `I have ceased to be disabled` `a day in the month I ceased to be disabled`) (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `I have started a retirement pension` `the first month for which my retirement pension is payable`) `my date of birth` (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `I have died` `the day they died`)

@export In which month am I treated as having applied for a retirement pension when my disability pension ends at 65 (s 70(2))?
GIVEN `my disability pension ends because I reached 65` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your disability pension end because you reached 65 (and not for an earlier reason)?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `In which month am I treated as having applied for a retirement pension when my disability pension ends at 65 (s 70(2))` IS
    `s 70(2) — the month in which an application for a retirement pension is deemed made by and received from the person` `my disability pension ends because I reached 65` `my date of birth`

@export From which month does the retirement pension I am treated as having applied for at 65 start (s 70(2))?
GIVEN `my disability pension ends because I reached 65` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your disability pension end because you reached 65 (and not for an earlier reason)?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From which month does the retirement pension I am treated as having applied for at 65 start (s 70(2))` IS
    `s 70(2) — the month with which the retirement pension applied for is to commence` `my disability pension ends because I reached 65` `my date of birth`

-- s 70(3). After a retirement pension has begun the person cannot apply (again) for a disability pension.
@export Am I barred from applying for a disability pension because I have started a retirement pension (s 70(3))?
GIVEN `I have started to receive a retirement pension under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you started to receive a retirement pension under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan?
      `I can cancel the retirement pension under section 66.1 or a substantially similar provincial provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 66.1 (cancelling a benefit), or a substantially similar provision of a provincial pension plan, apply to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred from applying for a disability pension because I have started a retirement pension (s 70(3))` IF
    `s 70(3) — the person is ineligible to apply or re-apply for a disability pension` `I have started to receive a retirement pension under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan` `I can cancel the retirement pension under section 66.1 or a substantially similar provincial provision`

-- s 70.01. The month a post-retirement disability benefit is first payable.
@export From which month is my post-retirement disability benefit payable (s 70.01)?
GIVEN `payment of my post-retirement disability benefit has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister approved payment of your post-retirement disability benefit?
      `a day in the month I became disabled` IS A DATE @desc In which month were you determined to have become disabled? (Any day in that month.)
      `I received a disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit in the five years before that month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At any time in the five years before the month you became disabled, did you receive a disability pension (under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan) or a post-retirement disability benefit?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From which month is my post-retirement disability benefit payable (s 70.01)` IS
    `s 70.01 — the month a post-retirement disability benefit is first payable` `payment of my post-retirement disability benefit has been approved` `a day in the month I became disabled` `I received a disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit in the five years before that month`

@export How many months before my application can I be treated as having become disabled, for a post-retirement disability benefit (s 70.01(b))?
GIVEN `I received a disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit in the five years before the month I became disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At any time in the five years before the month you became disabled, did you receive a disability pension (under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan) or a post-retirement disability benefit?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many months before my application can I be treated as having become disabled, for a post-retirement disability benefit (s 70.01(b))` IS
    `s 70.01(b) — the number of months to read in place of fifteen months in paragraph 42(2)(b)` `I received a disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit in the five years before the month I became disabled`

-- s 70.02. The last month for which a post-retirement disability benefit is paid.
@export Until which month is my post-retirement disability benefit paid (s 70.02)?
GIVEN `I have ceased to be disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ceased to be disabled?
      `a day in the month I ceased to be disabled` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you cease to be disabled? (Any day in it; ignored if you have not.)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `I have died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person who received the benefit died?
      `the day they died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did they die? (Ignored if not.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Until which month is my post-retirement disability benefit paid (s 70.02)` IS
    `s 70.02 — the last month for which a post-retirement disability benefit is payable` (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `I have ceased to be disabled` `a day in the month I ceased to be disabled`) `my date of birth` (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `I have died` `the day they died`)

-- 2007, c. 11, s. 36. Whether the rule on years of contributions in subparagraph 44(2)(a)(i.1) applies to the application.
@export Does the 25-year contribution test in subparagraph 44(2)(a)(i.1) apply to my application for a disability pension (2007, c. 11, s. 36)?
GIVEN `a day in the month I applied for the disability pension` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you apply for the disability pension? (Any day in that month.)
      `a day in the month section 2 of the 2007 amending Act came into force` IS A DATE @desc In which month did section 2 of S.C. 2007, c. 11 come into force? (A date from the Canada Gazette; the Act's text does not give it.)
      `I applied late and was found disabled earlier` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your disability pension one that would have been payable at the time you are deemed to have become disabled if you had applied earlier (subparagraph 44(1)(b)(ii))?
      `a day in the month I am deemed to have become disabled` IS A DATE @desc In which month are you deemed to have become disabled? (Any day in that month.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the 25-year contribution test in subparagraph 44(2)(a)(i.1) apply to my application for a disability pension (2007, c. 11, s. 36)` IF
    `RP 2007 c. 11 s 36 — subparagraph 44(2)(a)(i.1) applies in respect of the application` `a day in the month I applied for the disability pension` `a day in the month section 2 of the 2007 amending Act came into force` `I applied late and was found disabled earlier` `a day in the month I am deemed to have become disabled`

§§ `Getting a disability pension or benefit back after returning to work (reinstatement)`
-- Situation: you stopped receiving a disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit because you returned to work.

-- s 70.1(1), with 2004, c. 22, s. 23. Entitlement to reinstatement.
@export Am I entitled to have my disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit reinstated (s 70.1(1); 2004, c. 22, s. 23)?
GIVEN `I stopped receiving it because I returned to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you stop receiving your disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit because you returned to work?
      `a day in the month I stopped receiving it` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you stop receiving it? (Any day in that month.)
      `a day in the month I became incapable of working again` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you become incapable of working again? (Any day in that month.)
      `a day in the month section 20 of the 2004 amending Act came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did section 20 of S.C. 2004, c. 22 come into force? (A date from the Canada Gazette; the Act's text does not give it.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to have my disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit reinstated (s 70.1(1); 2004, c. 22, s. 23)` IF
        `s 70.1(1) — the person is entitled to have the disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit reinstated` `I stopped receiving it because I returned to work` `a day in the month I stopped receiving it` `a day in the month I became incapable of working again`
    AND (NOT (`RP 2004 c. 22 s 23 — section 70.1 does not apply in respect of the person` `I stopped receiving it because I returned to work` `a day in the month I stopped receiving it` `a day in the month section 20 of the 2004 amending Act came into force`))

-- s 70.1(2) with regulation 71. Whether the request for reinstatement is in time and in writing.
@export Is my request for reinstatement made in time and in writing (s 70.1(2); regulation 71)?
GIVEN `a day in the month I became incapable of working again` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you become incapable of working again? (Any day in that month.)
      `the day I made my request` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you make (or will you make) your request for reinstatement?
      `my request was made in writing to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your request made in writing to the Minister?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my request for reinstatement made in time and in writing (s 70.1(2); regulation 71)` IF
    `s 70.1(2) — the request for reinstatement was made in accordance with the regulations` `a day in the month I became incapable of working again` `the day I made my request` `my request was made in writing to the Minister`

-- s 70.1(3). The Minister shall approve the request if satisfied.
@export Must the Minister approve my request for reinstatement (s 70.1(3))?
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that my severe and prolonged disability is the same as, or related to, the disability that entitled me to the pension or benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister been satisfied that you have a severe and prolonged mental or physical disability that is the same as, or related to, the disability that entitled you to the disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit?
      `a day in the month I stopped receiving it` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you stop receiving the pension or benefit? (Any day in that month.)
      `a day in the month I became incapable of working again` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you become incapable of working again? (Any day in that month.)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `my request is for a disability pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your request for reinstatement of a disability pension (answer no if it is for a post-retirement disability benefit)?
      `I was receiving a retirement pension in the month I became incapable again` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you receiving a retirement pension in the month you became incapable of working again?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister approve my request for reinstatement (s 70.1(3))` IF
    `s 70.1(3) — the Minister must approve the request for reinstatement` `the Minister is satisfied that my severe and prolonged disability is the same as, or related to, the disability that entitled me to the pension or benefit` `a day in the month I stopped receiving it` `a day in the month I became incapable of working again` `my date of birth` `my request is for a disability pension` `I was receiving a retirement pension in the month I became incapable again`

-- s 70.1(4). My child's benefit is reinstated with my pension.
@export Must the Minister reinstate my child's disabled contributor's child benefit when my pension is reinstated (s 70.1(4))?
GIVEN `my pension or benefit is reinstated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your pension or benefit been reinstated under subsection 70.1(3)?
      `the Minister is satisfied that my child meets the requirements for a disabled contributor's child benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister been satisfied that your child meets the requirements under the Act for a disabled contributor's child benefit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister reinstate my child's disabled contributor's child benefit when my pension is reinstated (s 70.1(4))` IF
    `s 70.1(4) — the Minister must approve the reinstatement of the disabled contributor's child benefit` `my pension or benefit is reinstated` `the Minister is satisfied that my child meets the requirements for a disabled contributor's child benefit`

-- s 70.1(5) and (6). What the Minister owes the person in writing.
@export Must the Minister tell me in writing whether my request for reinstatement is approved (s 70.1(5))?
GIVEN `I made a request for reinstatement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a request for reinstatement of a disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister tell me in writing whether my request for reinstatement is approved (s 70.1(5))` IF
    `s 70.1(5) — the Minister must inform the person in writing of the decision whether or not to approve the request` `I made a request for reinstatement`

@export Must the Minister tell me in writing whether a disabled contributor's child benefit is approved on a reinstatement (s 70.1(6))?
GIVEN `I made the request for reinstatement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the request for reinstatement?
      `I am a child of the person who made the request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the child of the person who made the request?
      `I am a person or agency having decision-making responsibility for that child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person or agency referred to in section 75 in relation to that child (the one having decision-making responsibility, or whom the Minister has directed)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister tell me in writing whether a disabled contributor's child benefit is approved on a reinstatement (s 70.1(6))` IF
    `s 70.1(6) — the Minister must inform the person in writing of the decision whether or not to approve a disabled contributor's child benefit` `I made the request for reinstatement` `I am a child of the person who made the request` `I am a person or agency having decision-making responsibility for that child`

-- s 70.1(7) and (8). Which provisions of the Act apply to a reinstated pension, benefit or child's benefit.
@export Does a provision of the Act apply to my reinstated disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit (s 70.1(7))?
GIVEN provision IS A `cp5 Provision of the Act that section 70.1 may except` @desc Which provision are you asking about? One of: the provision paragraph 42(2)(b); the provision paragraph 44(1)(b); the provision paragraph 44(1)(e); the provision paragraph 44(1)(h); the provision paragraph 44(2)(a); the provision subsection 44(4); the provision subsection 74(2); the provision section 69; the provision section 70.01; another provision of the Act.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a provision of the Act apply to my reinstated disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit (s 70.1(7))` IF
    `s 70.1(7) — a provision of the Act applies to a reinstated disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit` provision

@export Does a provision of the Act apply to my reinstated disabled contributor's child benefit (s 70.1(8))?
GIVEN provision IS A `cp5 Provision of the Act that section 70.1 may except` @desc Which provision are you asking about? One of: the provision paragraph 42(2)(b); the provision paragraph 44(1)(b); the provision paragraph 44(1)(e); the provision paragraph 44(1)(h); the provision paragraph 44(2)(a); the provision subsection 44(4); the provision subsection 74(2); the provision section 69; the provision section 70.01; another provision of the Act.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a provision of the Act apply to my reinstated disabled contributor's child benefit (s 70.1(8))` IF
    `s 70.1(8) — a provision of the Act applies to a reinstated disabled contributor's child benefit` provision

-- s 70.1(9). The least the reinstated amount can be.
@export How much is my reinstated disability pension, or the survivor's pension I receive, per month at least (s 70.1(9))?
GIVEN `the monthly amount the rules of Part II give me without the minimum` IS A NUMBER @desc What monthly amount do the ordinary rules of Part II give for the reinstated pension, in dollars?
      `my last monthly amount before the pension ceased, adjusted annually under subsection 45(2)` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the monthly amount payable for the month before the pension ceased, adjusted each year as subsection 45(2) provides, in dollars?
      `my pensionable earnings have been divided under sections 55 to 55.3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under sections 55 to 55.3 been made that affects you?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is my reinstated disability pension, or the survivor's pension I receive, per month at least (s 70.1(9))` IS
    `s 70.1(9) — the monthly amount of the reinstated disability pension, or of the survivor's pension payable to the person` `the monthly amount the rules of Part II give me without the minimum` `my last monthly amount before the pension ceased, adjusted annually under subsection 45(2)` `my pensionable earnings have been divided under sections 55 to 55.3`

-- s 70.1(10). The month reinstated payments begin.
@export From which month is my reinstated pension or benefit paid (s 70.1(10))?
GIVEN `a day in the month I became incapable of working again` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you become incapable of working again? (Any day in that month.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From which month is my reinstated pension or benefit paid (s 70.1(10))` IS
    `s 70.1(10) — the month with which a reinstated pension or benefit is payable` `a day in the month I became incapable of working again`

§§ `Death benefit`
-- Situation: a contributor has died and a death benefit is payable.

-- s 71(2) and regulation 64(1). Whether the Minister may direct the death benefit to someone other than the estate.
@export May the Minister direct the death benefit to someone other than the estate (s 71(2); regulation 64(1))?
GIVEN `there is no estate, after reasonable inquiries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister been satisfied, after making reasonable inquiries, that the deceased contributor left no estate?
      `the day the contributor died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the contributor die?
      `the estate has applied for the death benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the estate applied for the death benefit?
      `the day the estate applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the estate apply? (Ignored if it has not.)
      `the day on which a direction would be considered` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the Minister consider giving a direction (today, if you are asking now)?
      `the amount of the death benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the death benefit, in dollars?
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year of the death` IS A NUMBER @desc For a death before 1998 only: what was the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year of the death, in dollars? (Enter 0 for a later death.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Minister direct the death benefit to someone other than the estate (s 71(2); regulation 64(1))` IF
    `s 71(2) — the Minister may direct payment of the death benefit in whole or in part to a prescribed person or body` `there is no estate, after reasonable inquiries` `the day the contributor died` (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `the estate has applied for the death benefit` `the day the estate applied`) `the day on which a direction would be considered` `the amount of the death benefit` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year of the death`

-- s 71(1). To whom the death benefit is paid.
@export To whom is the death benefit paid (s 71)?
GIVEN `payment of the death benefit has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister approved payment of the death benefit?
      `the Minister directs payment to someone other than the estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister directed payment to a prescribed person or body other than the estate?
      `there is no estate, after reasonable inquiries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister been satisfied, after making reasonable inquiries, that the deceased contributor left no estate?
      `the day the contributor died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the contributor die?
      `the estate has applied for the death benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the estate applied for the death benefit?
      `the day the estate applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the estate apply? (Ignored if it has not.)
      `the day on which a direction would be considered` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the Minister consider giving a direction (today, if you are asking now)?
      `the amount of the death benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the death benefit, in dollars?
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year of the death` IS A NUMBER @desc For a death before 1998 only: what was the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year of the death, in dollars? (Enter 0 for a later death.)
GIVETH A MAYBE `cp5 Payee of a death benefit`
DECIDE `To whom is the death benefit paid (s 71)` IS
    `s 71 — to whom the death benefit is paid` `payment of the death benefit has been approved` `the Minister directs payment to someone other than the estate` (`s 71(2) — the Minister may direct payment of the death benefit in whole or in part to a prescribed person or body` `there is no estate, after reasonable inquiries` `the day the contributor died` (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `the estate has applied for the death benefit` `the day the estate applied`) `the day on which a direction would be considered` `the amount of the death benefit` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year of the death`)

-- Regulation 64(1) to (3). Who may be directed to receive it, and how much to the person who paid the funeral.
@export To whom may the Minister direct the death benefit, in order (regulation 64(1))?
GIVEN `someone paid or is responsible for the funeral expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an individual or institution that has paid, or is responsible for paying, the deceased contributor's funeral expenses?
      `there is a survivor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the deceased contributor leave a survivor?
      `there is next of kin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the deceased contributor leave next of kin?
GIVETH A `cp5 Person or body to whom a death benefit may be directed`
DECIDE `To whom may the Minister direct the death benefit, in order (regulation 64(1))` IS
    `s 71(2) — the person or body to whom payment may be directed under regulation 64(1)` `someone paid or is responsible for the funeral expenses` `there is a survivor` `there is next of kin`

@export How much of the death benefit can go to me if I paid the funeral expenses (regulation 64(2))?
GIVEN `the amount of the death benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the death benefit, in dollars?
      `the actual funeral expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc What were the actual funeral expenses, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of the death benefit can go to me if I paid the funeral expenses (regulation 64(2))` IS
    `s 71(2) — the most that may be paid to the individual or institution who paid the funeral expenses under regulation 64(2)` `the amount of the death benefit` `the actual funeral expenses`

-- s 71(3). Once paid under subsection (2), the Minister owes no one else.
@export Can I still claim the death benefit for the contributor's estate after it was paid to someone else under subsection 71(2) (s 71(3))?
GIVEN `a payment has been made under subsection 71(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister paid the death benefit to a prescribed person or body under subsection 71(2)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I still claim the death benefit for the contributor's estate after it was paid to someone else under subsection 71(2) (s 71(3))` IF
    NOT (`s 71(3) — the Minister is not liable to make that payment to any subsequent applicant` `a payment has been made under subsection 71(2)`)

§§ `Survivor's pension`
-- Situation: a contributor has died and you are their survivor.

-- s 72. The first month a survivor's pension is paid.
@export From which month is my survivor's pension payable (s 72)?
GIVEN `payment of my survivor's pension has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister approved payment of your survivor's pension?
      `I am entitled under subparagraph 44(1)(d)(i) (before 2019)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to the survivor's pension under the rules for before 2019 (65 or older; or under 65 and either 35 or older at the death, caring for dependent children, or disabled)?
      `I am entitled under subparagraph 44(1)(d)(ii) (after 2018)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to the survivor's pension under the rule for after 2018 (any survivor of a contributor with enough contributions)?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day the contributor died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the contributor die?
      `I maintained dependent children of the contributor at the time of the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the contributor's death, were you a survivor who wholly or substantially maintained one or more of the contributor's dependent children?
      `I became disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you determined to be disabled?
      `the day I became disabled` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you become disabled? (Ignored if not.)
      `a day in the month my application was received` IS A DATE @desc In which month did the Minister receive your application for the survivor's pension? (Any day in that month.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From which month is my survivor's pension payable (s 72)` IS
    `s 72 — the first month for which a survivor's pension is payable` `payment of my survivor's pension has been approved` `I am entitled under subparagraph 44(1)(d)(i) (before 2019)` `I am entitled under subparagraph 44(1)(d)(ii) (after 2018)` `my date of birth` `the day the contributor died` `I maintained dependent children of the contributor at the time of the death` (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `I became disabled` `the day I became disabled`) `a day in the month my application was received`

-- s 73(1) and (3). How long a survivor's pension is paid, and when a division ends it.
@export Is my survivor's pension paid for a particular month (s 73)?
GIVEN `the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? (Any day in that month.)
      `the first month for which the pension is payable` IS A DATE @desc From which month is the survivor's pension payable? (Any day in that month.)
      `the beneficiary has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person who received the survivor's pension died?
      `the day the beneficiary died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did they die? (Ignored if not.)
      `a division of pensionable earnings between me and the contributor has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings between you and the contributor been approved under paragraph 55.1(1)(b)?
      `a day in the month the division takes effect` IS A DATE @desc In which month does the approved division take effect? (Any day in that month; ignored if none.)
      `I was cohabiting with the contributor in a new conjugal relationship when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When the contributor died, were you cohabiting with them in a new conjugal relationship?
      `the day our continuous cohabitation began` IS A DATE @desc On what day did that continuous cohabitation begin? (Ignored if you were not cohabiting.)
      `the day the contributor died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the contributor die?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my survivor's pension paid for a particular month (s 73)` IF
    `s 73 — a survivor's pension is paid for a month` `the month I am asking about` `the first month for which the pension is payable` (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `the beneficiary has died` `the day the beneficiary died`) (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `a division of pensionable earnings between me and the contributor has been approved` `a day in the month the division takes effect`) `I was cohabiting with the contributor in a new conjugal relationship when they died` `the day our continuous cohabitation began` `the day the contributor died`

-- s 73(2). A married survivor's right to continue is not affected by approving a common-law partner's pension.
@export Is my survivor's pension safe when a pension is approved for the contributor's common-law partner (s 73(2))?
GIVEN `the day the contributor died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the contributor die?
      `the day subsection 73(2) came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did subsection 73(2) come into force? (A date from the amending Act; the Act's text does not give it.)
      `I was married to the contributor and a survivor's pension was payable to me when that subsection came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you married to the contributor at the time of the death, and was a survivor's pension payable to you immediately before that subsection came into force?
      `the other survivor was the contributor's common-law partner and not a spouse under the old definition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person approved for a survivor's pension the contributor's common-law partner at the time of the death, and not a person described in paragraph (a)(ii) of the definition spouse as it then read?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my survivor's pension safe when a pension is approved for the contributor's common-law partner (s 73(2))` IS
    `s 73(2) — the approval of a survivor's pension to the common-law partner does not affect the right of the survivor who had been married to the contributor to continue to receive the survivor's pension` `the day the contributor died` `the day subsection 73(2) came into force` `I was married to the contributor and a survivor's pension was payable to me when that subsection came into force` `the other survivor was the contributor's common-law partner and not a spouse under the old definition`

@export Does my survivor's pension end because of a division of pensionable earnings (s 73(3))?
GIVEN `a division of pensionable earnings between me and the contributor has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings between you and the contributor been approved under paragraph 55.1(1)(b)?
      `a day in the month the division takes effect` IS A DATE @desc In which month does the approved division take effect? (Any day in that month; ignored if none.)
      `I was cohabiting with the contributor in a new conjugal relationship when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When the contributor died, were you cohabiting with them in a new conjugal relationship?
      `the day our continuous cohabitation began` IS A DATE @desc On what day did that continuous cohabitation begin? (Ignored if you were not cohabiting.)
      `the day the contributor died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the contributor die?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Does my survivor's pension end because of a division of pensionable earnings (s 73(3))` IS
    `s 73(3) — the last month for which a survivor's pension is paid because of a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings` (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `a division of pensionable earnings between me and the contributor has been approved` `a day in the month the division takes effect`) `I was cohabiting with the contributor in a new conjugal relationship when they died` `the day our continuous cohabitation began` `the day the contributor died`

§§ `Disabled contributor's child's benefit and orphan's benefit`
-- Situation: you are a child of a disabled contributor, or an orphan of a contributor, or you act for such a child.

-- s 74(1). Who may apply.
@export May I apply for the child's or orphan's benefit on the child's behalf (s 74(1))?
GIVEN `I am the child or orphan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the disabled contributor's child or the orphan?
      `I am a person or agency to whom the benefit would be paid if approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person or agency to whom the benefit would be payable, if the application were approved (for a child under 18, the person or agency with decision-making responsibility)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply for the child's or orphan's benefit on the child's behalf (s 74(1))` IF
    `s 74(1) — the application may be made on behalf of the disabled contributor's child or orphan by the applicant` `I am the child or orphan` `I am a person or agency to whom the benefit would be paid if approved`

-- s 74(2)(a) and (b). The first month the benefit is paid.
@export From which month is the disabled contributor's child's benefit payable (s 74(2)(a))?
GIVEN `payment of the benefit has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister approved payment of the disabled contributor's child's benefit?
      `the first month for which the contributor's disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit is payable` IS A DATE @desc From which month is the contributor's disability pension (under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan) or post-retirement disability benefit payable? (Any day in that month.)
      `a day in the month the child was born or became the contributor's child` IS A DATE @desc In which month was the child born, or otherwise became a child of the contributor? (Any day in that month.)
      `a day in the month the application was received` IS A DATE @desc In which month did the Minister receive the application? (Any day in that month.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From which month is the disabled contributor's child's benefit payable (s 74(2)(a))` IS
    `s 74(2)(a) — the first month for which a disabled contributor's child's benefit is payable` `payment of the benefit has been approved` `the first month for which the contributor's disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit is payable` `a day in the month the child was born or became the contributor's child` `a day in the month the application was received`

@export From which month is the orphan's benefit payable (s 74(2)(b))?
GIVEN `payment of the benefit has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister approved payment of the orphan's benefit?
      `a day in the month the contributor died` IS A DATE @desc In which month did the contributor die? (Any day in that month.)
      `a day in the month the child was born` IS A DATE @desc In which month was the child born? (Any day in that month.)
      `a day in the month the application was received` IS A DATE @desc In which month did the Minister receive the application? (Any day in that month.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From which month is the orphan's benefit payable (s 74(2)(b))` IS
    `s 74(2)(b) — the first month for which an orphan's benefit is payable` `payment of the benefit has been approved` `a day in the month the contributor died` `a day in the month the child was born` `a day in the month the application was received`

-- s 74(3) and (3.1). No benefit in respect of more than two contributors.
@export Is the child's or orphan's benefit barred in respect of this contributor (s 74(3))?
GIVEN `a child's or orphan's benefit has become payable to the child in respect of another contributor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan, has a disabled contributor's child's benefit or an orphan's benefit already become payable to the child in respect of another contributor?
      `the child is a child of this contributor within the meaning of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child a child of this contributor, within the meaning of the definition of child of a contributor in subsection 42(1) (so that the contributor is the child's parent)?
      `the number of contributors for whom such a benefit has been paid to the child` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many contributors has such a benefit already been paid to the child?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the child's or orphan's benefit barred in respect of this contributor (s 74(3))` IF
    `s 74(3) — the benefit is not payable to the person in respect of the contributor` `a child's or orphan's benefit has become payable to the child in respect of another contributor` (`s 74(3.1) — the person is a parent of the child` `the child is a child of this contributor within the meaning of the Act`) `the number of contributors for whom such a benefit has been paid to the child`

-- s 75(1). To whom the benefit is paid.
@export To whom is the child's or orphan's benefit paid (s 75(1))?
GIVEN `the child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is the child's date of birth?
      `the day on which the payee is decided` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the question asked (today, if now)?
      `someone has decision-making responsibility for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a person or agency having decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan?
GIVETH A MAYBE `cp5 Payee of a child's or orphan's benefit`
DECIDE `To whom is the child's or orphan's benefit paid (s 75(1))` IS
    `s 75(1) — to whom a disabled contributor's child's benefit or orphan's benefit is paid` `the child's date of birth` `the day on which the payee is decided` `someone has decision-making responsibility for the child`

-- s 75(2). Who is presumed to have decision-making responsibility.
@export Who is presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan (s 75(2))?
GIVEN `the benefit is an orphan's benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the benefit an orphan's benefit? (Answer no for a disabled contributor's child's benefit.)
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence that someone else has decision-making responsibility?
      `the contributor has a survivor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an orphan: did the contributor leave a survivor?
      `the percentage of the parenting time that the contributor or survivor has` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the parenting time in respect of the child does the contributor (for a disabled contributor's child) or the survivor (for an orphan) have?
GIVETH A `cp5 Person presumed to have decision-making responsibility`
DECIDE `Who is presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan (s 75(2))` IS
    `s 75(2) — the person presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan` `the benefit is an orphan's benefit` `there is evidence to the contrary` `the contributor has a survivor` `the percentage of the parenting time that the contributor or survivor has`

-- s 76(1) and regulation 65.1(b). When the disabled contributor's child's benefit ends.
@export Until which month is the disabled contributor's child's benefit paid (s 76(1))?
GIVEN `the child has ceased to be a dependent child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the child ceased to be a dependent child?
      `a day in the month the child ceased to be a dependent child` IS A DATE @desc In which month did the child cease to be a dependent child? (Any day in it; ignored if not.)
      `the child has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the child died?
      `a day in the month the child died` IS A DATE @desc In which month did the child die? (Any day in it; ignored if not.)
      `the contributor's disability pension or benefit has ceased for a reason other than reaching 65` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contributor's disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit ceased to be payable for a reason other than the contributor having reached 65?
      `a day in the month the contributor's pension or benefit ceased` IS A DATE @desc In which month did it cease? (Any day in it; ignored if not.)
      `the child was adopted by someone other than the contributor or the contributor's spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the child adopted, legally or in fact, by someone other than the disabled contributor or the contributor's spouse or common-law partner?
      `a day in the month of the adoption` IS A DATE @desc In which month was the child adopted? (Any day in it; ignored if not.)
      `the contributor makes financial provision for the child periodically` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the disabled contributor make financial provision for the child periodically?
      `the amount of the periodic provision` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is the periodic provision for the child, in dollars?
      `the disabled contributor's child's benefit payable` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is the disabled contributor's child's benefit payable under the Act, in dollars?
      `the contributor has ceased to have parenting time or decision-making responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the disabled contributor ceased to have parenting time or decision-making responsibility in respect of the child?
      `a day in the month the contributor ceased to have it` IS A DATE @desc In which month did the contributor cease to have it? (Any day in it; ignored if not.)
      `the child is a child only because of that parenting time or decision-making responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child a child as defined in subsection 42(1) by reason of the contributor having had that parenting time or decision-making responsibility?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Until which month is the disabled contributor's child's benefit paid (s 76(1))` IS
    `s 76(1) — the last month for which a disabled contributor's child's benefit is payable` (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `the child has ceased to be a dependent child` `a day in the month the child ceased to be a dependent child`) (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `the child has died` `a day in the month the child died`) (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `the contributor's disability pension or benefit has ceased for a reason other than reaching 65` `a day in the month the contributor's pension or benefit ceased`) (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `the child was adopted by someone other than the contributor or the contributor's spouse or common-law partner` `a day in the month of the adoption`) (`s 76(1)(d) — the disabled contributor is maintaining the child, as defined by regulation 65.1(b)` `the contributor makes financial provision for the child periodically` `the amount of the periodic provision` `the disabled contributor's child's benefit payable`) (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `the contributor has ceased to have parenting time or decision-making responsibility` `a day in the month the contributor ceased to have it`) `the child is a child only because of that parenting time or decision-making responsibility`

-- s 76(2) and (3).
@export Until which month is the orphan's benefit paid (s 76(2))?
GIVEN `the child has ceased to be a dependent child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the child ceased to be a dependent child?
      `a day in the month the child ceased to be a dependent child` IS A DATE @desc In which month did the child cease to be a dependent child? (Any day in it; ignored if not.)
      `the child has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the child died?
      `a day in the month the child died` IS A DATE @desc In which month did the child die? (Any day in it; ignored if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Until which month is the orphan's benefit paid (s 76(2))` IS
    `s 76(2) — the last month for which an orphan's benefit is payable` (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `the child has ceased to be a dependent child` `a day in the month the child ceased to be a dependent child`) (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `the child has died` `a day in the month the child died`)

@export In which month is my application for an orphan's benefit treated as made when a disabled contributor's child's benefit ceases because of the contributor's death (s 76(3))?
GIVEN `my disabled contributor's child's benefit ceases because of the contributor's death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your disabled contributor's child's benefit cease to be payable because of the death of a contributor?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day the contributor died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the contributor die?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `In which month is my application for an orphan's benefit treated as made when a disabled contributor's child's benefit ceases because of the contributor's death (s 76(3))` IS
    `s 76(3) — the month in which an application for an orphan's benefit is deemed made by the person` `my disabled contributor's child's benefit ceases because of the contributor's death` `my date of birth` `the day the contributor died`

§§ `Post-retirement benefit`
-- Situation: you receive a retirement pension and still work and contribute.

-- s 76.1 and 76.2.
@export From which month will I receive a post-retirement benefit for my earnings (s 76.1)?
GIVEN `I receive a retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a beneficiary of a retirement pension under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan?
      `a contribution was made on those earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a contribution made in respect of those earnings?
      `my earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your earnings for the period, in dollars?
      `my basic exemption` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic exemption for the year, in dollars?
      `the first day of the period of those earnings` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the period of those earnings begin?
      `the last day of the period of those earnings` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the period of those earnings end?
      `the first month for which my retirement pension is payable` IS A DATE @desc From which month was your retirement pension payable? (Any day in that month.)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the year of those earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc In which calendar year did you earn them?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From which month will I receive a post-retirement benefit for my earnings (s 76.1)` IS
    `s 76.1 — the first month for which a post-retirement benefit is payable` `I receive a retirement pension` `a contribution was made on those earnings` `my earnings` `my basic exemption` `the first day of the period of those earnings` `the last day of the period of those earnings` `the first month for which my retirement pension is payable` `my date of birth` `the year of those earnings`

@export Until which month is the post-retirement benefit paid (s 76.2)?
GIVEN `the beneficiary has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person who receives the post-retirement benefit died?
      `the day the beneficiary died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did they die? (Ignored if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Until which month is the post-retirement benefit paid (s 76.2)` IS
    `s 76.2 — the last month for which a post-retirement benefit is paid` (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `the beneficiary has died` `the day the beneficiary died`)

§§ `How much of a benefit is paid under the Canada Pension Plan, and not under a provincial pension plan`
-- Situation: you have contributed both to the Canada Pension Plan and to a provincial pension plan (the Quebec Pension Plan).
-- The totals asked below are figures from your Statement of Contributions or the Minister; the person cannot work them out unaided.

-- s 77. The proportion payable under the Act.
@export What proportion of my benefit is paid under the Canada Pension Plan (s 77)?
GIVEN `my total pensionable earnings attributable to base contributions made under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your total pensionable earnings attributable to base contributions made under the Canada Pension Plan Act, in dollars?
      `my total first additional pensionable earnings attributable to first additional contributions made under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your total first additional pensionable earnings attributable to first additional contributions made under the Act, in dollars?
      `my total second additional pensionable earnings attributable to second additional contributions made under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your total second additional pensionable earnings attributable to second additional contributions made under the Act, in dollars?
      `my total pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your total pensionable earnings, in dollars?
      `my total first additional pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your total first additional pensionable earnings, in dollars?
      `my total second additional pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your total second additional pensionable earnings, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What proportion of my benefit is paid under the Canada Pension Plan (s 77)` IS
    `s 77 — the proportion of a benefit that is payable under this Act` `my total pensionable earnings attributable to base contributions made under the Act` `my total first additional pensionable earnings attributable to first additional contributions made under the Act` `my total second additional pensionable earnings attributable to second additional contributions made under the Act` `my total pensionable earnings` `my total first additional pensionable earnings` `my total second additional pensionable earnings`

-- s 77 and s 80. The amount payable under the Act.
@export How much of my monthly benefit is paid under the Canada Pension Plan, in dollars (ss 77 and 80)?
GIVEN `the amount of my benefit before section 77` IS A NUMBER @desc What monthly amount of the benefit do the rules of Part II give, ignoring section 77, in dollars?
      `my proportion payable under the Act is known` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know the proportion of your benefit payable under the Act (section 77)?
      `the proportion payable under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What is that proportion, as a fraction between 0 and 1? (Ignored if you do not know it.)
      `an agreement with a province puts the whole benefit under` IS A `cp5 Where an agreement under section 80 puts the whole of a benefit` @desc Does an agreement under section 80 put the whole of the benefit under one plan? One of: no agreement under section 80 puts the whole of the benefit under one plan; an agreement under section 80 puts the whole of the benefit under this Act; an agreement under section 80 puts the whole of the benefit under the provincial pension plan.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my monthly benefit is paid under the Canada Pension Plan, in dollars (ss 77 and 80)` IS
    `s 77 and s 80 — the amount of the benefit that is payable under this Act` `the amount of my benefit before section 77` (IF `my proportion payable under the Act is known` THEN JUST `the proportion payable under the Act` ELSE NOTHING) `an agreement with a province puts the whole benefit under`

-- ss 78 and 79, 78.1 and 79.1, 78.2 and 79.2. The share of a year's pensionable earnings counted under the Act.
@export What share of my base unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year counts under the Canada Pension Plan (ss 78 and 79)?
GIVEN `my earnings for the year on which a base contribution was made under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc In that year, on how much of your earnings was a base contribution made under the Canada Pension Plan, in dollars?
      `my earnings for the year on which a base contribution was made under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc In that year, on how much of your earnings was a base contribution made under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
      `that year is a year of a division of pensionable earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that year a year of a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings (sections 55 and 55.1)?
      `my base unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to me by the division` IS A NUMBER @desc For a year of a division: how much of your base unadjusted pensionable earnings was attributed to you by the division, in dollars? (Ignored otherwise.)
      `the total base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year determined for the division` IS A NUMBER @desc For a year of a division: what is the total base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year determined for the division, in dollars? (Ignored otherwise.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What share of my base unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year counts under the Canada Pension Plan (ss 78 and 79)` IS
    `cp5 helper -- the proportion that applies to a year of one tier` year
    WHERE
        year MEANS `cp5 Year of earnings of one tier` WITH
            -- Placeholder: the proportion does not read the amount of the unadjusted pensionable earnings.
            `unadjusted pensionable earnings of the tier for the year` IS 0
            `earnings on which a contribution of the tier has been made for the year under this Act` IS `my earnings for the year on which a base contribution was made under the Act`
            `earnings on which a contribution of the tier has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS `my earnings for the year on which a base contribution was made under a provincial pension plan`
            `the year is a year of a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings` IS `that year is a year of a division of pensionable earnings`
            `unadjusted pensionable earnings of the tier attributed by the division` IS `my base unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to me by the division`
            `total unadjusted pensionable earnings of the tier for the year determined for the division` IS `the total base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year determined for the division`

@export What share of my first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year counts under the Canada Pension Plan (ss 78.1 and 79.1)?
GIVEN `my earnings for the year on which a first additional contribution was made under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc In that year, on how much of your earnings was a first additional contribution made under the Canada Pension Plan, in dollars?
      `my earnings for the year on which a first additional contribution was made under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc In that year, on how much of your earnings was a first additional contribution made under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
      `that year is a year of a division of pensionable earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that year a year of a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings (section 55.1)?
      `my first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to me by the division` IS A NUMBER @desc For a year of a division: how much of your first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings was attributed to you by the division, in dollars? (Ignored otherwise.)
      `the total first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year determined for the division` IS A NUMBER @desc For a year of a division: what is the total first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year determined for the division, in dollars? (Ignored otherwise.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What share of my first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year counts under the Canada Pension Plan (ss 78.1 and 79.1)` IS
    `cp5 helper -- the proportion that applies to a year of one tier` year
    WHERE
        year MEANS `cp5 Year of earnings of one tier` WITH
            -- Placeholder: the proportion does not read the amount of the unadjusted pensionable earnings.
            `unadjusted pensionable earnings of the tier for the year` IS 0
            `earnings on which a contribution of the tier has been made for the year under this Act` IS `my earnings for the year on which a first additional contribution was made under the Act`
            `earnings on which a contribution of the tier has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS `my earnings for the year on which a first additional contribution was made under a provincial pension plan`
            `the year is a year of a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings` IS `that year is a year of a division of pensionable earnings`
            `unadjusted pensionable earnings of the tier attributed by the division` IS `my first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to me by the division`
            `total unadjusted pensionable earnings of the tier for the year determined for the division` IS `the total first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year determined for the division`

@export What share of my second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year counts under the Canada Pension Plan (ss 78.2 and 79.2)?
GIVEN `my earnings for the year on which a second additional contribution was made under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc In that year, on how much of your earnings was a second additional contribution made under the Canada Pension Plan, in dollars?
      `my earnings for the year on which a second additional contribution was made under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc In that year, on how much of your earnings was a second additional contribution made under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
      `that year is a year of a division of pensionable earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that year a year of a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings (section 55.1)?
      `my second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to me by the division` IS A NUMBER @desc For a year of a division: how much of your second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings was attributed to you by the division, in dollars? (Ignored otherwise.)
      `the total second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year determined for the division` IS A NUMBER @desc For a year of a division: what is the total second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year determined for the division, in dollars? (Ignored otherwise.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What share of my second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year counts under the Canada Pension Plan (ss 78.2 and 79.2)` IS
    `cp5 helper -- the proportion that applies to a year of one tier` year
    WHERE
        year MEANS `cp5 Year of earnings of one tier` WITH
            -- Placeholder: the proportion does not read the amount of the unadjusted pensionable earnings.
            `unadjusted pensionable earnings of the tier for the year` IS 0
            `earnings on which a contribution of the tier has been made for the year under this Act` IS `my earnings for the year on which a second additional contribution was made under the Act`
            `earnings on which a contribution of the tier has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS `my earnings for the year on which a second additional contribution was made under a provincial pension plan`
            `the year is a year of a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings` IS `that year is a year of a division of pensionable earnings`
            `unadjusted pensionable earnings of the tier attributed by the division` IS `my second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributed to me by the division`
            `total unadjusted pensionable earnings of the tier for the year determined for the division` IS `the total second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year determined for the division`

-- s 80.1(3) and (4). An agreement that apportions disability benefits with a workers' compensation or similar scheme.
-- Situation: an agreement under subsection 80.1(1) applies to you.
@export Is the agreement that apportions my disability benefit within the limits the Act sets (s 80.1(4))?
GIVEN `the agreement changes my eligibility for, or the amount of, a disabled contributor's child's benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement change anyone's eligibility to receive a benefit as a disabled contributor's child, or the amount of that benefit?
      `the agreement changes which months are excluded from my contributory period for disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement change the determination of months excluded from a beneficiary's contributory period by reason of disability?
      `the disability benefit the agreement makes payable under the Act for the month` IS A NUMBER @desc What disability benefit under the Canada Pension Plan Act does the agreement make payable for the month, in dollars?
      `the payments under the other law or activity for the month` IS A NUMBER @desc What payments are made for the month under the other law or activity, in dollars?
      `the disability benefit otherwise payable under the Act for the month` IS A NUMBER @desc What disability benefit would be payable under the Canada Pension Plan Act for the month if there were no agreement, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the agreement that apportions my disability benefit within the limits the Act sets (s 80.1(4))` IF
    `s 80.1(4) — the agreement is within the limits that subsection (4) sets` `the agreement changes my eligibility for, or the amount of, a disabled contributor's child's benefit` `the agreement changes which months are excluded from my contributory period for disability` `the disability benefit the agreement makes payable under the Act for the month` `the payments under the other law or activity for the month` `the disability benefit otherwise payable under the Act for the month`

@export How much disability benefit is payable under the Canada Pension Plan for the month when an agreement applies to me (s 80.1(3))?
GIVEN `an agreement under subsection 80.1(1) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an agreement under subsection 80.1(1) (apportioning disability benefits between the Act and another law or activity) apply to you?
      `the agreement is within the limits of subsection 80.1(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement within the limits of subsection 80.1(4)?
      `the amount the agreement provides payable under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount does the agreement provide is payable under the Canada Pension Plan Act for the month, in dollars?
      `the disability benefit otherwise payable under the Act for the month` IS A NUMBER @desc What disability benefit would be payable under the Act for the month if there were no agreement, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much disability benefit is payable under the Canada Pension Plan for the month when an agreement applies to me (s 80.1(3))` IS
    `s 80.1(3) — the disability benefit payable under this Act for the month` `an agreement under subsection 80.1(1) applies to me` `the agreement is within the limits of subsection 80.1(4)` `the amount the agreement provides payable under the Act` `the disability benefit otherwise payable under the Act for the month`

§§ `Asking the Minister to reconsider a decision, and appealing`
-- Situation: you are dissatisfied with a decision or determination about your benefit, a division of pensionable earnings, or a penalty.

-- s 81(1). Who may ask, and about which decisions.
@export May I ask the Minister to reconsider this decision or determination (s 81(1))?
GIVEN `I am` IS A `cp5 Person dissatisfied under subsection 81(1)` @desc Which are you? One of: a spouse, former spouse, common-law partner, former common-law partner or estate dissatisfied under paragraph 81(1)(a); an applicant dissatisfied under paragraph 81(1)(b); a beneficiary dissatisfied under paragraph 81(1)(c) or (d); a beneficiary's spouse or common-law partner dissatisfied under paragraph 81(1)(d); a person who made a request under section 70.1, a child of that person or, in relation to that child, a person or agency referred to in section 75, dissatisfied under paragraph 81(1)(e); a person to whom none of paragraphs 81(1)(a) to (e) refers.
      `the decision or determination is` IS A `cp5 Decision or determination of subsection 81(1)` @desc Which decision or determination is it? One of: a decision made under section 55, 55.1, 55.2 or 55.3 that subsection 81(1) names; a decision made under section 60 that subsection 81(1) names; a determination as to the amount of a benefit payable to the beneficiary or as to the beneficiary's eligibility to receive a benefit that subsection 81(1) names; a decision made under section 65.1 that subsection 81(1) names; a decision made under section 70.1 that subsection 81(1) names; a decision that subsection 81(1) does not name.
      `I am dissatisfied with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you dissatisfied with the decision or determination?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask the Minister to reconsider this decision or determination (s 81(1))` IF
    `s 81(1) — the person is a dissatisfied party who may ask the Minister to reconsider the decision or determination` `I am` `the decision or determination is` `I am dissatisfied with it`

@export May someone else make the request for reconsideration for me (s 81(1))?
GIVEN `the person is the dissatisfied party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person making the request the dissatisfied party themself?
      `the regulations allow the person to act for the dissatisfied party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations allow this person to make the request for the dissatisfied party (for example, a person authorized by law to manage the affairs of someone who cannot manage their own)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May someone else make the request for reconsideration for me (s 81(1))` IF
    `s 81(1) — the person may make the request for the dissatisfied party` `the person is the dissatisfied party` `the regulations allow the person to act for the dissatisfied party`

-- s 81(1) and (1.1) with regulations 74.1(3) and (4), 74.2. Am I in time?
@export Was I notified of the decision in the way the regulations require (s 81(1); regulation 74.2)?
GIVEN `the notice was in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice of the decision or determination in writing?
      `the notice was sent by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice sent by the Minister?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I notified of the decision in the way the regulations require (s 81(1); regulation 74.2)` IF
    `s 81(1) — the person was notified in the prescribed manner under regulation 74.2` `the notice was in writing` `the notice was sent by the Minister`

@export By what day must I ask the Minister to reconsider (s 81(1) and (1.1))?
GIVEN `I was notified in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you notified of the decision or determination in the manner the regulations require (in writing, sent by the Minister)?
      `the day I was notified` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you notified? (Ignored if you were not notified in the prescribed manner.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I ask the Minister to reconsider (s 81(1) and (1.1))` IS
    `s 81(1) and (1.1) — the last day of the ninety days for the request` (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `I was notified in the prescribed manner` `the day I was notified`)

@export Is my request for reconsideration made in time (s 81(1) and (1.1))?
GIVEN `I was notified in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you notified of the decision or determination in the manner the regulations require (in writing, sent by the Minister)?
      `the day I was notified` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you notified? (Ignored if you were not notified in the prescribed manner.)
      `the Minister allowed me a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister allow you a period longer than the ninety days (before or after the ninety days ran out)?
      `the last day of that longer period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the longer period? (Ignored if none.)
      `the day I make my request` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you make (or will you make) your request?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my request for reconsideration made in time (s 81(1) and (1.1))` IF
    `s 81(1) and (1.1) — the request for reconsideration is made in time` (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `I was notified in the prescribed manner` `the day I was notified`) (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `the Minister allowed me a longer period` `the last day of that longer period`) `the day I make my request`

@export May the Minister allow me a longer period to ask for reconsideration (s 81(1); regulation 74.1(3) and (4))?
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied there is a reasonable explanation for my asking late` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister been satisfied that there is a reasonable explanation for your requesting a longer period?
      `I have shown a continuing intention to ask for reconsideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you shown a continuing intention to request a reconsideration?
      `more than 365 days have passed since I was notified in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your request made more than 365 days after the day you were notified in writing of the decision or determination?
      `I have applied again for the same benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied again for the same benefit?
      `I have asked the Minister to rescind or amend the decision under subsection 81(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you asked the Minister to rescind or amend the decision under subsection 81(3)?
      `the Minister is satisfied my request has a reasonable chance of success` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister been satisfied that your request for reconsideration has a reasonable chance of success?
      `the Minister is satisfied no prejudice would be caused by the longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister been satisfied that no prejudice would be caused to the Minister or a party by allowing a longer period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Minister allow me a longer period to ask for reconsideration (s 81(1); regulation 74.1(3) and (4))` IF
    `s 81(1) — the Minister may allow a longer period to make the request, under regulation 74.1(3) and (4)` `the Minister is satisfied there is a reasonable explanation for my asking late` `I have shown a continuing intention to ask for reconsideration` `more than 365 days have passed since I was notified in writing` `I have applied again for the same benefit` `I have asked the Minister to rescind or amend the decision under subsection 81(3)` `the Minister is satisfied my request has a reasonable chance of success` `the Minister is satisfied no prejudice would be caused by the longer period`

@export Is my request for reconsideration in the form the regulations require (s 81(1); regulation 74.1(1))?
GIVEN `my request is in writing to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your request in writing, to the Minister?
      `it sets out the contributor's name, address and Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out the name, address and Social Insurance Number of the contributor?
      `I am the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the contributor?
      `it sets out my name, address and relationship to the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out your name and address and your relationship to the contributor? (Needed only if you are not the contributor.)
      `it sets out the grounds and the facts they rest on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out the grounds for the request and a statement of the facts that form its basis?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my request for reconsideration in the form the regulations require (s 81(1); regulation 74.1(1))` IF
    `s 81(1) — the request is made in the prescribed form and manner of regulation 74.1(1)` `my request is in writing to the Minister` `it sets out the contributor's name, address and Social Insurance Number` `I am the contributor` `it sets out my name, address and relationship to the contributor` `it sets out the grounds and the facts they rest on`

-- s 81(1.1). A penalty assessed under section 90.1.
@export May I ask the Minister to reconsider the penalty assessed on me (s 81(1.1))?
GIVEN `a penalty has been assessed on me under section 90.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a penalty been assessed on you under section 90.1?
      `I am dissatisfied with the decision to impose it or its amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you dissatisfied with the decision to impose the penalty, or with its amount?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask the Minister to reconsider the penalty assessed on me (s 81(1.1))` IF
    `s 81(1.1) — the person may ask the Minister to reconsider the decision to impose a penalty or its amount` `a penalty has been assessed on me under section 90.1` `I am dissatisfied with the decision to impose it or its amount`

-- s 81(2) and (3). What the Minister owes after a request, and may do on new facts.
@export What must the Minister do and tell me after I ask for a reconsideration (s 81(2))?
GIVEN `I have made a request for reconsideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a request for reconsideration under subsection 81(1) or (1.1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `What must the Minister do and tell me after I ask for a reconsideration (s 81(2))` IF
    `s 81(2) — the Minister must reconsider the decision or determination without delay and notify the requester in writing of the decision and of the reasons for it` `I have made a request for reconsideration`

@export Can the Minister rescind or amend a decision made about me (s 81(3))?
GIVEN `there are new facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there new facts since the decision was made?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Minister rescind or amend a decision made about me (s 81(3))` IF
    `s 81(3) — the Minister may rescind or amend the decision` `there are new facts`

-- s 82. Appeal to the Social Security Tribunal. The time for the appeal is in the Department of Employment and Social Development Act (not among the texts read).
@export May I appeal the Minister's decision on my reconsideration to the Social Security Tribunal (s 82)?
GIVEN `I am dissatisfied with the Minister's decision on my reconsideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you dissatisfied with a decision of the Minister made under section 81 (including a decision on whether to allow you further time to ask for a reconsideration)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I appeal the Minister's decision on my reconsideration to the Social Security Tribunal (s 82)` IF
    `s 82 — the party may appeal the decision of the Minister to the Social Security Tribunal` `I am dissatisfied with the Minister's decision on my reconsideration`

-- s 83. After a Tribunal decision the Minister may stay payment.
@export Until what day may the Minister stay payment of my benefit after a Tribunal decision (s 83)?
GIVEN `the Social Security Tribunal has made a decision about my benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Social Security Tribunal made a decision in respect of your benefit?
      `the last day to apply for leave to appeal to the Appeal Division` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period allowed for applying for leave to appeal to the Appeal Division of the Tribunal?
      `the last day to apply for judicial review` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period allowed for applying under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of the decision?
      `Her Majesty has applied for judicial review` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has Her Majesty (the Crown) applied under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of the decision?
      `a day in the month all the judicial review proceedings were completed` IS A DATE @desc In which month were all the proceedings in relation to the judicial review completed? (Any day in that month; ignored if the Crown has not applied.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Until what day may the Minister stay payment of my benefit after a Tribunal decision (s 83)` IS
    `s 83 — the last day to which the Minister may stay payment of the benefit` `the Social Security Tribunal has made a decision about my benefit` `the last day to apply for leave to appeal to the Appeal Division` `the last day to apply for judicial review` (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `Her Majesty has applied for judicial review` `a day in the month all the judicial review proceedings were completed`)

§§ `Census information and presumed death`

-- s 87. The Minister may use old census returns to find a person's age.
@export May the Minister get my age from old census returns (s 87; regulation 51)?
GIVEN `the purpose is to ascertain the age of an applicant or beneficiary or of their spouse, common-law partner, former spouse or former common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose to ascertain the age of an applicant or beneficiary, or of their spouse, common-law partner, former spouse or former common-law partner?
      `the day the census was taken` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the census taken?
      `the day of the request` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the request to Statistics Canada made?
      `the request is in the form the Chief Statistician prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the request made in a form prescribed by the Chief Statistician?
      `the request bears the signed consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request bear the signed consent of the person (or of the person or agency who applied on their behalf)?
      `the request gives the information needed for a proper search` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request give the information needed to enable a proper search of the census records?
      `the information obtained will not be disclosed except as the regulation allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will the information obtained be disclosed only to officers, clerks or employees of the Department of Employment and Social Development, or as an agreement under section 105 requires?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Minister get my age from old census returns (s 87; regulation 51)` IF
    `s 87 — the Minister is entitled to obtain from Statistics Canada the information about the person's age that the census returns contain` `the purpose is to ascertain the age of an applicant or beneficiary or of their spouse, common-law partner, former spouse or former common-law partner` `the day the census was taken` `the day of the request` (`s 87 — the conditions prescribed by regulation 51 are met` `the request is in the form the Chief Statistician prescribes` `the request bears the signed consent` `the request gives the information needed for a proper search` `the information obtained will not be disclosed except as the regulation allows`)

-- s 88. Presumption as to death.
-- Situation: a contributor, beneficiary or their spouse or common-law partner has disappeared.
@export From which date is a contributor, beneficiary or spouse of mine who has disappeared treated as having died (s 88(1))?
GIVEN `the person is a contributor or beneficiary, or the spouse or common-law partner of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who disappeared a contributor or beneficiary, or the spouse, common-law partner, former spouse or former common-law partner of one?
      `the Minister is of the opinion that the disappearance raises beyond a reasonable doubt a presumption of death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the Minister's opinion that the person disappeared under circumstances that raise beyond a reasonable doubt a presumption that the person is dead?
      `the Minister has determined a date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister determined the date on which the person's death is presumed to have occurred?
      `the date the Minister determined` IS A DATE @desc What date did the Minister determine? (Ignored if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From which date is a contributor, beneficiary or spouse of mine who has disappeared treated as having died (s 88(1))` IS
    `s 88(1) — the date on which the person is deemed to have died` `the person is a contributor or beneficiary, or the spouse or common-law partner of one` `the Minister is of the opinion that the disappearance raises beyond a reasonable doubt a presumption of death` (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `the Minister has determined a date` `the date the Minister determined`)

@export From which date is the person treated as having died once the Minister determines a different date (s 88(2))?
GIVEN `the Minister has determined a date of death under subsection 88(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister determined a date of death under subsection 88(1)?
      `the Minister is satisfied by new information that the date is different` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied from new information or evidence that the date of death is different?
      `the Minister has determined a different date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister determined a different date of death?
      `the different date` IS A DATE @desc What is the different date? (Ignored if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From which date is the person treated as having died once the Minister determines a different date (s 88(2))` IS
    `s 88(2) — the date on which the person is deemed to have died after the Minister determines a different date` `the Minister has determined a date of death under subsection 88(1)` `the Minister is satisfied by new information that the date is different` (`cp5 seat helper -- a day that may not apply` `the Minister has determined a different date` `the different date`)

@export Must the Minister pay me the benefit I would have been paid had the death not been presumed (s 88(2) and (3))?
GIVEN `the Minister has determined a different date of death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister determined a different date of death under subsection 88(2)?
      `the Minister has determined a date of death under subsection 88(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister determined a date of death under subsection 88(1)?
      `the Minister is satisfied from new information that the person is alive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied from new information or evidence that the person is alive?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister pay me the benefit I would have been paid had the death not been presumed (s 88(2) and (3))` IF
        `s 88(2) — the Minister must forthwith cause to be paid any benefit that would have been payable if the determination of death had not been made` `the Minister has determined a different date of death`
     OR `s 88(3) — the Minister must forthwith cause to be paid any benefit that would have been payable in respect of the person had the determination not been made` `the Minister has determined a date of death under subsection 88(1)` `the Minister is satisfied from new information that the person is alive`

@export Must a benefit paid to me because another person was presumed dead stop once the Minister is satisfied that person is alive (s 88(4))?
GIVEN `a benefit was paid to me as a result of the determination of another person's death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a benefit paid to you as a result of the Minister's determination of another person's death under section 88?
      `the Minister is satisfied from new information that the other person is alive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied from new information or evidence that the other person is alive?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must a benefit paid to me because another person was presumed dead stop once the Minister is satisfied that person is alive (s 88(4))` IF
    `s 88(4) — the benefit ceases forthwith to be payable` `a benefit was paid to me as a result of the determination of another person's death` `the Minister is satisfied from new information that the other person is alive`

@export Do I keep what I was paid before the Minister was satisfied that the other person is alive (s 88(4))?
GIVEN `a benefit was paid to me as a result of the determination of another person's death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a benefit paid to you as a result of the Minister's determination of another person's death under section 88?
      `the Minister is satisfied from new information that the other person is alive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied from new information or evidence that the other person is alive?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I keep what I was paid before the Minister was satisfied that the other person is alive (s 88(4))` IF
    `s 88(4) — the benefit paid before the Minister was satisfied that the other person is alive is deemed to have been validly paid` `a benefit was paid to me as a result of the determination of another person's death` `the Minister is satisfied from new information that the other person is alive`

@export Does a death certificate issued or revoked by another authority bind the Minister in deciding on my benefit (s 88(5))?
GIVEN `another authority has issued or revoked a death certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has another authority issued or revoked a death certificate for the person?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a death certificate issued or revoked by another authority bind the Minister in deciding on my benefit (s 88(5))` IF
    `s 88(5) — the Minister is bound by the issuance or revocation of a death certificate by another authority` `another authority has issued or revoked a death certificate`

§§ `False statements, offences and penalties`
-- Situation: you made a statement or application that was false or misleading, or received a benefit payment that was not due, and the Minister has noticed.

-- s 90(1). Whether the conduct is an offence.
@export Have I committed an offence under the Act by what I said or did (s 90(1))?
GIVEN `I knowingly made a false or misleading statement in an application or declaration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly make a false or misleading statement in an application or declaration?
      `I made an application or declaration that is false or misleading because I did not disclose facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make an application or declaration that, by reason of non-disclosure of facts, is false or misleading?
      `I obtained a benefit payment by false pretences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain a benefit payment by false pretences?
      `as payee I negotiated or tried to negotiate a cheque for a benefit I was not entitled to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As payee, did you negotiate or attempt to negotiate a cheque for a benefit to which you were not entitled?
      `I knowingly failed to return a cheque, payment or excess amount that section 66 required me to return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly fail to return a cheque, the amount of a benefit payment or an excess amount, as section 66 required?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed an offence under the Act by what I said or did (s 90(1))` IF
    `s 90(1) — the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` `I knowingly made a false or misleading statement in an application or declaration` `I made an application or declaration that is false or misleading because I did not disclose facts` `I obtained a benefit payment by false pretences` `as payee I negotiated or tried to negotiate a cheque for a benefit I was not entitled to` `I knowingly failed to return a cheque, payment or excess amount that section 66 required me to return`

-- s 90(2). The last day for proceedings.
@export By what day can proceedings be started against me for an offence (s 90(2))?
GIVEN `the day the Minister became aware of the subject-matter of the proceedings` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Minister become aware of the subject-matter of the proceedings?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day can proceedings be started against me for an offence (s 90(2))` IS
    `s 90(2) — the last day on which proceedings in respect of an offence may be commenced` `the day the Minister became aware of the subject-matter of the proceedings`

@export Can proceedings still be started against me for the offence on a given day (s 90(2))?
GIVEN `the day the Minister became aware of the subject-matter of the proceedings` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Minister become aware of the subject-matter of the proceedings?
      `the day the proceedings would be started` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the proceedings be started?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can proceedings still be started against me for the offence on a given day (s 90(2))` IF
    `s 90(2) — proceedings in respect of the offence may be commenced on that day` `the day the Minister became aware of the subject-matter of the proceedings` `the day the proceedings would be started`

-- s 90(3). Penalty or prosecution, not both.
@export Am I protected from prosecution for an act or omission for which a penalty was imposed on me (s 90(3))?
GIVEN `a penalty for that act or omission was imposed on me under section 90.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a penalty for that act or omission imposed on you under section 90.1?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I protected from prosecution for an act or omission for which a penalty was imposed on me (s 90(3))` IF
    `s 90(3) — no proceeding shall be commenced under section 90 or the Criminal Code for the act or omission` `a penalty for that act or omission was imposed on me under section 90.1`

-- s 90.1(1) to (4). Administrative monetary penalties.
@export Can the Minister impose a penalty on me for what I said or did (s 90.1(1))?
GIVEN `the Minister has become aware of facts that in the Minister's opinion establish an act or omission by me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister become aware of facts that, in the Minister's opinion, establish that you did one of the acts or omissions below?
      `I made a statement or declaration that I knew was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a statement or declaration, in an application or otherwise, that you knew was false or misleading?
      `I made a statement or declaration that I knew was misleading because I did not disclose facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a statement or declaration, in an application or otherwise, that you knew was false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts?
      `I knowingly failed to declare my earnings for a period when I received disability benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly fail to declare to the Minister all or some of your earnings for a period for which you received disability benefits?
      `I received a benefit payment I knew I was not entitled to and did not return it without delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive or obtain a benefit payment that you knew you were not entitled to (or that you knew was more than you were entitled to) and not return it, or the excess, without delay?
      `I participated in, assented to or acquiesced in such an act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you participate in, assent to or acquiesce in an act or omission of those kinds?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Minister impose a penalty on me for what I said or did (s 90.1(1))` IF
    `s 90.1(1) — the Minister may impose a penalty on the person` `the Minister has become aware of facts that in the Minister's opinion establish an act or omission by me` `I made a statement or declaration that I knew was false or misleading` `I made a statement or declaration that I knew was misleading because I did not disclose facts` `I knowingly failed to declare my earnings for a period when I received disability benefits` `I received a benefit payment I knew I was not entitled to and did not return it without delay` `I participated in, assented to or acquiesced in such an act or omission`

@export What is the most the Minister can set as the penalty on me, in dollars (s 90.1(2))?
GIVEN `the number of acts or omissions` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many acts or omissions is the penalty being set?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most the Minister can set as the penalty on me, in dollars (s 90.1(2))` IS
    `s 90.1(2) — the most the Minister may set as the penalty for the acts or omissions` `the number of acts or omissions`

@export Is the penalty set on me within the maximum for each act or omission (s 90.1(2))?
GIVEN `the amount set as the penalty for the act or omission` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount has been set as the penalty for the act or omission, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the penalty set on me within the maximum for each act or omission (s 90.1(2))` IF
    `s 90.1(2) — the amount set for the act or omission is within the maximum` `the amount set as the penalty for the act or omission`

@export Is it too late for the Minister to impose a penalty on me (s 90.1(3))?
GIVEN `a prosecution for the act or omission has been started against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a prosecution for the act or omission been initiated against you?
      `the day the Minister became aware of the act or omission` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Minister become aware of the act or omission?
      `the day the penalty would be imposed` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the penalty be imposed (today, if you are asking now)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it too late for the Minister to impose a penalty on me (s 90.1(3))` IF
    `s 90.1(3) — a penalty shall not be imposed on the person` `a prosecution for the act or omission has been started against me` `the day the Minister became aware of the act or omission` `the day the penalty would be imposed`

@export Can the Minister rescind or reduce the penalty imposed on me (s 90.1(4))?
GIVEN `new facts have been presented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have new facts been presented?
      `the Minister is satisfied the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on a mistake about, a material fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on the basis of a mistake as to, some material fact?
      `the Minister is satisfied the penalty cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the penalty cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future?
      `the Minister is satisfied payment would cause undue hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that payment of the penalty would cause undue hardship to the debtor?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Minister rescind or reduce the penalty imposed on me (s 90.1(4))` IF
    `s 90.1(4) — the Minister may rescind the imposition of the penalty, or reduce it` `new facts have been presented` `the Minister is satisfied the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on a mistake about, a material fact` `the Minister is satisfied the penalty cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future` `the Minister is satisfied payment would cause undue hardship`

§§ `The Minister's inspections and demands for documents or information`
-- Situation: the Minister has asked to enter your premises, examine documents, or has served you with a notice requiring information.

-- s 90.2(2)(a) and (3). May the Minister enter?
@export May the Minister enter my premises (s 90.2(2)(a) and (3))?
GIVEN `it is a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a reasonable time for the Minister to enter?
      `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose related to the administration or enforcement of the Canada Pension Plan Act?
      `the Minister believes a document about someone's entitlement to a benefit or its amount is or should be kept here` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister believe that a document relating to a person's entitlement to a benefit, or the amount of a benefit, is or should be kept at the premises or place?
      `the place is my dwelling-house` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place a dwelling-house (a residence, including a building connected to it by a doorway or covered, enclosed passageway, and a mobile unit used as a residence)?
      `I consent to the Minister's entering` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you, as occupant, consent to the Minister's entering?
      `a judge has issued a warrant to enter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a judge issued a warrant under subsection 90.2(4) authorizing the entry?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Minister enter my premises (s 90.2(2)(a) and (3))` IF
    `s 90.2(2)(a) — the Minister may enter the premises or place` `it is a reasonable time` `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of the Act` `the Minister believes a document about someone's entitlement to a benefit or its amount is or should be kept here` `the place is my dwelling-house` `I consent to the Minister's entering` `a judge has issued a warrant to enter`

-- s 90.2(2)(b). Assistance and attendance.
@export Must I give the Minister assistance, answer questions and attend at the premises (s 90.2(2)(b))?
GIVEN `it is a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a reasonable time?
      `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose related to the administration or enforcement of the Canada Pension Plan Act?
      `the Minister believes a document about someone's entitlement to a benefit or its amount is or should be kept here` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister believe that a document relating to a person's entitlement to a benefit, or the amount of a benefit, is or should be kept at the premises or place?
      `I am the owner, occupant or person in charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give the Minister assistance, answer questions and attend at the premises (s 90.2(2)(b))` IF
    `s 90.2(2)(b) — the person must give the Minister all reasonable assistance, answer all proper questions and attend at the place` `it is a reasonable time` `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of the Act` `the Minister believes a document about someone's entitlement to a benefit or its amount is or should be kept here` `I am the owner, occupant or person in charge`

-- s 90.2(4) and (5). What a judge may do about my dwelling-house.
@export Can a judge issue a warrant allowing the Minister to enter my dwelling-house (s 90.2(4))?
GIVEN `the Minister has applied without notice to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister applied ex parte (without notice to you)?
      `the judge is satisfied there are reasonable grounds to believe the dwelling-house is a place where documents are kept` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the dwelling-house is a premises or place referred to in subsection 90.2(2)?
      `the judge is satisfied entry is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied by information on oath that entry is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of the Act?
      `the judge is satisfied entry has been or will be refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied by information on oath that entry has been refused, or that there are reasonable grounds to believe it will be refused?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a judge issue a warrant allowing the Minister to enter my dwelling-house (s 90.2(4))` IF
    `s 90.2(4) — a judge may issue a warrant authorizing the Minister to enter the dwelling-house` `the Minister has applied without notice to me` `the judge is satisfied there are reasonable grounds to believe the dwelling-house is a place where documents are kept` `the judge is satisfied entry is necessary` `the judge is satisfied entry has been or will be refused`

@export Can a judge order me to give the Minister access to a document in my dwelling-house (s 90.2(5))?
GIVEN `the judge is not satisfied that entry is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge not satisfied that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of the Act?
      `the judge is satisfied access to a document has been or may be refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that access to a document that is or should be kept in the dwelling-house has been refused or may be expected to be refused?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a judge order me to give the Minister access to a document in my dwelling-house (s 90.2(5))` IF
    `s 90.2(5) — a judge may order the occupant to provide the Minister with reasonable access to the document and make any other appropriate order` `the judge is not satisfied that entry is necessary` `the judge is satisfied access to a document has been or may be refused`

-- s 90.2(6) and (7). A notice requiring information or a document.
@export Must I provide the information or document the Minister's notice requires by the time it stipulates (s 90.2(6) and (7))?
GIVEN `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose related to the administration or enforcement of the Canada Pension Plan Act?
      `the notice was served on me personally or by confirmed delivery service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice served on you personally or by confirmed delivery service?
      `the notice gives a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice stipulate a reasonable time to provide the information or document?
      `the requirement relates to one or more unnamed persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the requirement relate to one or more persons who are not named?
      `a judge has authorized the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a judge authorized the Minister to impose the requirement, under subsection 90.2(8)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I provide the information or document the Minister's notice requires by the time it stipulates (s 90.2(6) and (7))` IF
    `s 90.2(6) — the person must provide the information or document within the time stipulated in the notice` `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of the Act` `the notice was served on me personally or by confirmed delivery service` `the notice gives a reasonable time` (`s 90.2(7) — the Minister may impose the requirement on the third party` `the requirement relates to one or more unnamed persons` `a judge has authorized the requirement`)

@export Can a judge authorize the Minister to demand information about unnamed persons from me (s 90.2(8))?
GIVEN `the Minister has applied without notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister applied ex parte?
      `the judge is satisfied the person or group is ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied by information on oath that the person or group is ascertainable?
      `the judge is satisfied the requirement verifies compliance with a duty under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied by information on oath that the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with a duty or obligation under the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a judge authorize the Minister to demand information about unnamed persons from me (s 90.2(8))` IF
    `s 90.2(8) — a judge may authorize the Minister to impose the requirement on the third party` `the Minister has applied without notice` `the judge is satisfied the person or group is ascertainable` `the judge is satisfied the requirement verifies compliance with a duty under the Act`

@export Must the Minister serve the judge's authorization on me with the notice (s 90.2(9))?
GIVEN `an authorization was granted under subsection 90.2(8)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an authorization granted under subsection 90.2(8)?
      `the authorization was served together with the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the authorization served on you together with the notice?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister serve the judge's authorization on me with the notice (s 90.2(9))` IF
    `s 90.2(9) — the authorization has been served as the subsection requires` `an authorization was granted under subsection 90.2(8)` `the authorization was served together with the notice`

@export By what day can I apply for a review of the judge's authorization (s 90.2(10))?
GIVEN `the day the notice was served on me` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice served on you?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day can I apply for a review of the judge's authorization (s 90.2(10))` IS
    `s 90.2(10) — the last day on which the third party may apply for a review of the authorization` `the day the notice was served on me`

@export Can I still apply for a review of the judge's authorization on a given day (s 90.2(10))?
GIVEN `an authorization was granted under subsection 90.2(8)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an authorization granted under subsection 90.2(8)?
      `the day the notice was served on me` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice served on you?
      `the day I would apply` IS A DATE @desc On what day would you apply for the review?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I still apply for a review of the judge's authorization on a given day (s 90.2(10))` IF
    `s 90.2(10) — the third party may apply for a review of the authorization` `an authorization was granted under subsection 90.2(8)` `the day the notice was served on me` `the day I would apply`

@export Can the judge cancel the authorization when I ask for a review (s 90.2(11))?
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied the person or group is ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On the review, is the judge satisfied that the person or group is ascertainable?
      `the judge is satisfied the requirement verifies compliance with a duty under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On the review, is the judge satisfied that the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with a duty or obligation under the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the judge cancel the authorization when I ask for a review (s 90.2(11))` IF
    `s 90.2(11) — the judge may cancel the authorization previously granted` `the judge is satisfied the person or group is ascertainable` `the judge is satisfied the requirement verifies compliance with a duty under the Act`

-- s 90.2(12) and (13).
@export Is a certified copy of a document taken under section 90.2 evidence against me (s 90.2(12))?
GIVEN `the document was inspected, examined or provided under section 90.2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the document inspected, examined or provided in accordance with section 90.2?
      `a certified copy was made by the person who inspected it or to whom it was provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a certified copy made, or caused to be made, by the person who inspected or examined the document or to whom it was provided?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a certified copy of a document taken under section 90.2 evidence against me (s 90.2(12))` IF
    `s 90.2(12) — the copy is evidence of the nature and content of the original document and has the same probative force` `the document was inspected, examined or provided under section 90.2` `a certified copy was made by the person who inspected it or to whom it was provided`

@export Am I forbidden to interfere with someone doing what section 90.2 authorizes (s 90.2(13))?
GIVEN `I interfered with, or prevented or tried to prevent, a person doing something` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you interfere with a person, or prevent or attempt to prevent them, from doing something?
      `section 90.2 authorized that person to do it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that person authorized under section 90.2 to do it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I forbidden to interfere with someone doing what section 90.2 authorizes (s 90.2(13))` IF
    `s 90.2(13) — the person contravened the prohibition on interfering with or preventing a person doing what section 90.2 authorizes` `I interfered with, or prevented or tried to prevent, a person doing something` `section 90.2 authorized that person to do it`
